<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.731 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.731 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.4 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due March 6, 1997 was 2.731 percent, up from 2.690 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.4 billion of 182-day T-bills due June 5, 1997 was 2.883 percent, up from 2.871 percent last week, and on C$1.0 billion of 357-day T-bills due November 27 was 3.208 percent, up from 3.167 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$700 million three-month, C$225 million six-month and C$150 million one-year bills. It holds C$1.2 billion of C$7.4 billion bills due Dec. 12 (Details follow)  </p>
